  "historical_0_3_record_description": "The record this vector's session produced before every producer moved to record_version \"0.4\", kept with the bytes, record_hash and producer_signature it had. It is a HISTORICAL ATTESTATION and MUST NOT be regenerated: nothing derives it, and re-sealing it under today's version would destroy the only thing it proves. That thing is Section 9A.2's additive recognizer -- a SessionEvidenceRecord sealed under an earlier version stays valid, because every such record is producer-sealed over its own record_version and so has no unbound tier to be downgraded to. This is the deliberate opposite of the TransactionRecord's clean break in the same release. expected.record is the same session's record at \"0.4\" and differs from this one in exactly three members: record_version, record_hash, and the producer_signature over that hash.",
